rvest\n- calculateNumberOfHungryStudents\n\nTo make this easier to test, you can simply drag the function blocks outside the start block to test other code on its own.\n\nNow it's your turn to create your own learning activity. Remember that we have learnt how to:\n- Ask for a player's name and store it in a setting (the program remembers it for next time)\n- Used the story extension with player choices to enable the player to select a correct answer\n- Ask for a number and use maths blocks to calculate a correct maths answer\n- Used images and long text to explore narrative themes of food waste and hunger</comment><data>{\"commentRefs\":[],\"fieldData\":{\"~commentOffsetX\":\"-422.8888888888889\",\"~commentOffsetY\":\"-10.666666666666664\"}}</data><statement name=\"HANDLER\"><block type=\"function_call\"><mutation name=\"getAndDisplayPlayerName\" functionid=\"f/yMxBA,mM}a2#,T1Y}8\"></mutation><next><block type=\"function_call\"><mutation name=\"WelcomeToOzHarvest\" functionid=\"|^@3!]3i{7!em?)KQ]VO\"></mutation><next><block type=\"function_call\"><mutation name=\"calculateNumberOfHungryStudents\" functionid=\"HT_BJM5W,K}eGae4^hU^\"></mutation></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"-1217\" y=\"-50\"><mutation name=\"calculateNumberOfHungryStudents\" functionid=\"HT_BJM5W,K}eGae4^hU^\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">calculateNumberOfHungryStudents</field><comment pinned=\"true\" h=\"555\" w=\"406\">This next part of the game uses \"ask for number\" (instead of \"ask for string\"), to get the player to input a number instead.\n\nAfter getting the number of students in the class, the program also asks for the number of hungry students in the class\n(1 in 9)\n\nThen the program calculates the number of hungry students by using maths blocks (floor and /)\n\nFinally the program checks if the answer is correct, and displays a correct or incorret message.</comment><data>{\"commentRefs\":[],\"fieldData\":{\